<pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="Ibdc28af48e37165832e49a9d7e96aab030e35578" commit="693bbd5802b071cc523edea86399bee25109fd4f" commit_message="CHROMIUM: mac80211: fix a kernel panic due to index outof bound.  * use signed int to store sigend value which is then used as an index into   array. * re enable rx stats. * collect rx stats for data frames only.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:51285 TEST=run  assoc/disassoc test from a 11ac sta 100 times.  Change-Id: Ibdc28af48e37165832e49a9d7e96aab030e35578 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/333875 Commit-Ready: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mohammed Shafi Shajakhan &lt;mohammed@qti.qualcomm.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Mohammed Shafi Shajakhan &lt;mohammed@qti.qualcomm.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Zhifeng Cai &lt;caiz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Grant Grundler &lt;grundler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="333875" owner_email="sduvvuri@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/75/333875/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia96ca4de919b178302580c23f911bb6445016285" commit="3af0b11ce026cb343d3e49c999ae2bbef089cb1c" commit_message="[autotest] Support run_suite with suite package and SSP for Brillo.  This change allows one to run run_suite command without using --run_prod_code for Brillo build. create_suite_job will use test_suites and control_files packages from the Brillo build to create suite job and its test jobs.  Server-side packaging is also supported for newer builds that have autotest_server_package artifact build.  BUG=chromium:584705 TEST=run in local instance, unittest, verify in moblab  Change-Id: Ia96ca4de919b178302580c23f911bb6445016285 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/332431 Commit-Ready: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="332431" owner_email="dshi@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/31/332431/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I019f37755faa4aa0fb6f7f4fe3f1e6306d282891" commit="71a8e2bb36d5626176b0c0cd482182736ccdbc83" commit_message="interleave_stereo use fmul then rounding float to int cast.  The current code rounds by adding or subtracting 0.5. This CL improves performance by multiplying the float by 32k, then using a rounding float to int conversion.  Was fcmgt interleave   NEON size =   4096, elapsed time = 203 ms Now fmul interleave   NEON size =   4096, elapsed time = 150 ms  BUG=none TEST=local unittest  Change-Id: I019f37755faa4aa0fb6f7f4fe3f1e6306d282891 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/332813 Commit-Ready: Frank Barchard &lt;fbarchard@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Frank Barchard &lt;fbarchard@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Frank Barchard &lt;fbarchard@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="332813" owner_email="fbarchard@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/13/332813/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I1100bcdffad45eb30f9be4a36c58dc8744579587" commit="8b304c4bef9f4621649534fe3322ed2d6f230d63" commit_message="UPSTREAM: genetlink: synchronize socket closing and family removal  In addition to the problem Jeff Layton reported, I looked at the code and reproduced the same warning by subscribing and removing the genl family with a socket still open. This is a fairly tricky race which originates in the fact that generic netlink allows the family to go away while sockets are still open - unlike regular netlink which has a module refcount for every open socket so in general this cannot be triggered.  Trying to resolve this issue by the obvious locking isn't possible as it will result in deadlocks between unregistration and group unbind notification (which incidentally lockdep doesn't find due to the home grown locking in the netlink table.)  To really resolve this, introduce a &quot;closing socket&quot; reference counter (for generic netlink only, as it's the only affected family) in the core netlink code and use that in generic netlink to wait for all the sockets that are being closed at the same time as a generic netlink family is removed.  This fixes the race that when a socket is closed, it will should call the unbind, but if the family is removed at the same time the unbind will not find it, leading to the warning. The real problem though is that in this case the unbind could actually find a new family that is registered to have a multicast group with the same ID, and call its mcast_unbind() leading to confusing.  Also remove the warning since it would still trigger, but is now no longer a problem.  This also moves the code in af_netlink.c to before unreferencing the module to avoid having the same problem in the normal non-genl case.  BUG=chromium:596019 TEST=run syzkaller on KASAN kernel  Signed-off-by: Johannes Berg &lt;johannes.berg@intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: David S. Miller &lt;davem@davemloft.net&gt; (cherry picked from commit ee1c244219fd652964710a6cc3e4f922e86aa492) Signed-off-by: Alexander Potapenko &lt;glider@google.com&gt;  Change-Id: I1100bcdffad45eb30f9be4a36c58dc8744579587 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/333910 Commit-Ready: Alexander Potapenko &lt;glider@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Alexander Potapenko &lt;glider@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Grant Grundler &lt;grundler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="333910" owner_email="glider@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/10/333910/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic4eea84983b98ad056ea9cd22be707617177ed7a" commit="fc5b32446b70c899b6931101f05cf3074609cbfb" commit_message="build_image_util: clarify failure message  If build_image fails, it will output a list of the largest files in the destination rootfs disk. The message is confusing because it does not make clear that these are files in the *destination* directory rather than the source, and that they made be partially files extracted if the untar died in the middle of a file. Clarify this.  BUG=None TEST=None  Change-Id: Ic4eea84983b98ad056ea9cd22be707617177ed7a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/333789 Commit-Ready: Aviv Keshet &lt;akeshet@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Aviv Keshet &lt;akeshet@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Chris Sosa &lt;sosa@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="333789" owner_email="akeshet@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/crosutils" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/crosutils" ref="refs/changes/89/333789/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I57adc26969df717438d0b7853ed3fae0dfb93807" commit="dc954a0c7679156164cb306d90e3ca26fcc041ed" commit_message="kernel_ConfigVerify: CONFIG_EXT4_USE_FOR_EXT23 removed in kernel v4.4  The upstream config setting was removed as of kernel v4.4, so only check for it in kernels older than it, to prevent it failing finding &quot;None&quot; for it on kernel v4.4.  BUG=chromium:574533 TEST=`test_that -b samus 100.107.3.13 suite:bvt-inline` on a host   running kernel-next/chromeos-4.4.   Before this commit:     results-32-kernel_ConfigVerify [  FAILED  ]     results-32-kernel_ConfigVerify FAIL: &quot;CONFIG_EXT4_USE_FOR_EXT23&quot; was &quot;None&quot; (wanted one of &quot;y&quot;) in kernel config   After this commit:     results-32-kernel_ConfigVerify [  PASSED  ]  Change-Id: I57adc26969df717438d0b7853ed3fae0dfb93807 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/334042 Commit-Ready: Filipe Brandenburger &lt;filbranden@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Filipe Brandenburger &lt;filbranden@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Olof Johansson &lt;olofj@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="334042" owner_email="filbranden@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/42/334042/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If2cf89cd27ef20b8dd8ec94f3d2b6a286d36189f" commit="59f1c30faf636f8c1d5ee0e8e2301fd1ad34bae0" commit_message="[autotest] teach test_push to wait 10s after closing a bug  Teach test_push script to wait 10s rather than 5s when closing a bug.  BUG=chromium:595230 TEST=Test locally  Change-Id: If2cf89cd27ef20b8dd8ec94f3d2b6a286d36189f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/334099 Commit-Ready: Shuqian Zhao &lt;shuqianz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shuqian Zhao &lt;shuqianz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="334099" owner_email="shuqianz@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/99/334099/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib3c5b8094798cb4df85f75f90329a1e988d08796" commit="b76ddbdca48689e7d4c6140a1f86267b62bceebe" commit_message="histogram_verifier: clarify failure message  The word &quot;bucket&quot; is vague, since we often use it to refer to google storage (GS) buckets. That makes this failure message smell a little like an infrastructure issue at first glance, even though it isn't. Clarify it.  BUG=None TEST=None  Change-Id: Ib3c5b8094798cb4df85f75f90329a1e988d08796 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/334041 Commit-Ready: Aviv Keshet &lt;akeshet@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Aviv Keshet &lt;akeshet@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Todd Broch &lt;tbroch@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="334041" owner_email="akeshet@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/41/334041/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib59c1caf71bae0b96a4c5b49e84a39fe6d7efdba" commit="c6549cd4e621c0bdbb6679a9c8d510b3d6347e86" commit_message="init: Trigger selected cros-ec sensors early  Commit 08b9bee05729099b026bccf4a1aeb74fd37d22c7 adds cros-ec devices to udev-trigger-early in order to trigger cros-ec sensors before ui loads. However, triggering with sysname-match only matches the platform devices but not the iio devices, thus the udev rules matching the iio devices may not be executed on platforms with built-in cros-ec* modules.  Add a trigger using attr-match for selected cros-ec sensors to udev-trigger-early. Currently only cros-ec-accel is listed.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:50851 TEST=Build and deploy chromeos-init to oak. Reboot and make sure      cros-ec-accel udev rules are triggered before ui starts.  Change-Id: Ib59c1caf71bae0b96a4c5b49e84a39fe6d7efdba Signed-off-by: Ricky Liang &lt;jcliang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/333884 Commit-Ready: Gwendal Grignou &lt;gwendal@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Gwendal Grignou &lt;gwendal@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Gwendal Grignou &lt;gwendal@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; Re